   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Supporter Grid\n\nA thank-you lockup for backers: a heart draws itself, pulses and docks upward while supporter avatars blur-stagger into a grid, then a headline, a supporter count and a call-to-action pill arrive.\n\nCategory: social. Length: 9 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A thank-you beat for funders or backers: the heart draws itself, docks upward, and every supporter avatar staggers into a grid.\n- A funding ask needs to end on a call-to-action pill and a link line.\n- The grid and the \"Powered by N supporters\" line should size themselves to a supporter list.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The milestone is a count that climbs (stars, followers): use star-counter or followers-overview.\n- The subject is one person's profile instead of a group of supporters: use profile-follow-card.\n- You need a neutral partner or integration lineup without the heart and CTA: use logo-enter.\n\nVariables:\n- supporters (string): Supporters, default \"Ada, Ben, Chloe, Dev, Eli, Fay, Gus, Hana, Ivo, June, Kai, Lena, Milo, Nia, Omar, Pia, Quin, Rhea, Sol, Tess, Uma, Vik, Wren, Zoe\"\n- heading (string): Heading, default \"Thank you\"\n- subline (string): Subline, default \"Powered by {count} supporters\"\n- cta_label (string): Button label, default \"Become a supporter\"\n- link_text (string): Link line, default \"example.org/support\"\n- accent_color (color): Accent, default \"#f97316\"\n- theme (enum): Theme, default \"light\"\n- transparent (boolean): Transparent, default false\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Supporter Grid\n\n  A thank-you lockup for backers: a heart draws itself, pulses and docks upward while supporter avatars blur-stagger into a grid, then a headline, a supporter count and a call-to-action pill arrive.\n\n  Adapted as an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/github-sponsors/index.tsx\n  The motion follows the source (heart draw and dock, avatar stagger, blur-in headline, CTA pill). The look was made generic: no product name, brand colour or lettering; avatars are initial discs built from a supporter list, and the link line and labels are variables.\n\n  MIT License\n\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"supporter-grid\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"9\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"supporters\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Supporters\", \"description\": \"Comma-separated names; each becomes an initial avatar and the count feeds the \\\"Powered by\\\" line.\", \"default\": \"Ada, Ben, Chloe, Dev, Eli, Fay, Gus, Hana, Ivo, June, Kai, Lena, Milo, Nia, Omar, Pia, Quin, Rhea, Sol, Tess, Uma, Vik, Wren, Zoe\"},\n    {\"id\": \"heading\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Heading\", \"description\": \"Headline that blurs in under the grid.\", \"default\": \"Thank you\"},\n    {\"id\": \"subline\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Subline\", \"description\": \"Line under the heading; {count} becomes the number of supporters.\", \"default\": \"Powered by {count} supporters\"},\n    {\"id\": \"cta_label\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Button label\", \"description\": \"Text of the call-to-action pill.\", \"default\": \"Become a supporter\"},\n    {\"id\": \"link_text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Link line\", \"description\": \"Small muted line under the button. Leave empty to hide it.\", \"default\": \"example.org/support\"},\n    {\"id\": \"accent_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Accent\", \"description\": \"Colour of the heart and the button.\", \"default\": \"#f97316\"},\n    {\"id\": \"theme\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Theme\", \"description\": \"Light or dark neutral theme.\", \"default\": \"light\", \"options\": [\n    {\"value\": \"light\", \"label\": \"Light\"},\n    {\"value\": \"dark\", \"label\": \"Dark\"}\n  ]},\n    {\"id\": \"transparent\", \"type\": \"boolean\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Transparent\", \"description\": \"Leave the background clear so the lockup sits over your own scene.\", \"default\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed multiplier; above 1 the scene plays faster and holds the end.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.05}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Supporter Grid</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute; inset: 0; overflow: hidden; container-type: size; pointer-events: none;\n          background: var(--sg-bg, #fff); color: var(--sg-fg, #171717);\n          font-family: Manrope, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", sans-serif;\n          -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;\n        }\n        #root * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n        .sg-clip { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n        .sg-stage { position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 50%; transform-origin: 50% 50%; }\n        .sg-av { position: absolute; border-radius: 50%; border: 1px solid var(--sg-border); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 600; color: #fff; will-change: transform, opacity, filter; }\n        .sg-heart { position: absolute; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .sg-line { position: absolute; left: 0; text-align: center; white-space: nowrap; }\n        .sg-w { display: inline-block; transform-origin: 50% 55%; }\n        .sg-c { display: inline-block; white-space: pre; transform-origin: 50% 55%; }\n        .sg-cta { position: absolute; left: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 12px; }\n        .sg-pill { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; padding: 14px 26px; border-radius: 9999px; color: #fff; font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; background: var(--sg-accent); }\n        .sg-link { font-size: 18px; color: var(--sg-muted); }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"supporter-grid\" data-duration=\"9\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"sg-clip\" class=\"sg-clip clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"9\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"sg-stage\" class=\"sg-stage\"></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var stage = document.getElementById(\"sg-stage\");\n            var vars = window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables() || {} : {};\n\n            var FPS = 30;\n            function num(v, d, min, max) { var n = Number(v); return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : d; }\n            function txt(v, d) { return typeof v === \"string\" ? v : d; }\n            function str(v, d) { return typeof v === \"string\" && v.trim() ? v : d; }\n            function colr(v, d) { return typeof v === \"string\" && v.trim() && window.CSS && CSS.supports(\"color\", v.trim()) ? v.trim() : d; }\n            function bool(v, d) { return v === true || v === \"true\" ? true : v === false || v === \"false\" ? false : d; }\n            function clamp(x, a, b) { return Math.min(b, Math.max(a, x)); }\n            function spring(frame, c) {\n              var t = Math.max(0, frame) / FPS, w0 = Math.sqrt(c.stiffness / c.mass), z = c.damping / (2 * Math.sqrt(c.stiffness * c.mass));\n              if (z < 1) { var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z); return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + (z * w0 / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t)); }\n              if (z === 1) return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n              var s = w0 * Math.sqrt(z * z - 1), r1 = -z * w0 + s, r2 = -z * w0 - s;\n              return 1 - (r2 * Math.exp(r1 * t) - r1 * Math.exp(r2 * t)) / (r2 - r1);\n            }\n            function el(tag, cls, parent, html) { var e = document.createElement(tag); if (cls) e.className = cls; if (html !== undefined) e.innerHTML = html; if (parent) parent.appendChild(e); return e; }\n\n            function bez(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              return function (x) {\n                if (x <= 0) return 0; if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                for (var i = 0; i < 32; i++) {\n                  t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                  var cx = 3 * (1 - t) * (1 - t) * t * x1 + 3 * (1 - t) * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                  if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                }\n                return 3 * (1 - t) * (1 - t) * t * y1 + 3 * (1 - t) * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n              };\n            }\n            var EASE_OUT = bez(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1), EASE_IN = bez(0.64, 0, 0.78, 0);\n            // the source framework-style interpolate on two points, clamped, with an easing.\n            function interp(x, a, b, from, to, ease) { var p = clamp((x - a) / (b - a), 0, 1); if (ease) p = ease(p); return from + (to - from) * p; }\n\n            var HEART = \"M12.0001 4.52853C14.2745 2.23823 17.9866 2.23823 20.2611 4.52853C22.5784 6.86156 22.5784 10.667 20.2611 13.0001L12.0001 21.3199L3.73907 13.0001C1.42175 10.667 1.42175 6.86156 3.73907 4.52853C6.01353 2.23823 9.72563 2.23823 12.0001 4.52853Z\";\n            var names = txt(vars.supporters, \"\").split(\",\").map(function (s) { return s.trim(); }).filter(Boolean);\n            if (!names.length) names = [\"Ada\", \"Ben\", \"Chloe\", \"Dev\", \"Eli\", \"Fay\", \"Gus\", \"Hana\", \"Ivo\", \"June\", \"Kai\", \"Lena\", \"Milo\", \"Nia\", \"Omar\", \"Pia\", \"Quin\", \"Rhea\", \"Sol\", \"Tess\", \"Uma\", \"Vik\", \"Wren\", \"Zoe\"];\n            names = names.slice(0, 120);\n            var heading = txt(vars.heading, \"Thank you\").trim();\n            var subline = txt(vars.subline, \"Powered by {count} supporters\").replace(\"{count}\", names.length).trim();\n            var ctaLabel = txt(vars.cta_label, \"Become a supporter\").trim();\n            var linkText = txt(vars.link_text, \"example.org/support\").trim();\n            var accent = colr(vars.accent_color, \"#f97316\");\n            var dark = String(vars.theme) === \"dark\";\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 4);\n            var T = dark ? { bg: \"#0b0b0d\", subtle: \"#17171a\", fg: \"#fafafa\", muted: \"#a1a1aa\", border: \"#2a2a30\" }\n                         : { bg: \"#ffffff\", subtle: \"#fafafa\", fg: \"#171717\", muted: \"#737373\", border: \"#ededed\" };\n            Object.keys(T).forEach(function (k) { root.style.setProperty(\"--sg-\" + k, T[k]); });\n            root.style.setProperty(\"--sg-accent\", accent);\n            if (bool(vars.transparent, false)) root.style.background = \"transparent\";\n\n            var W = root.clientWidth || 1080, H = root.clientHeight || 1920, portrait = H > W;\n            var RW = portrait ? 720 : 1280, RH = portrait ? 1280 : 720, k = Math.min(W / RW, H / RH);\n            stage.style.width = RW + \"px\"; stage.style.height = RH + \"px\";\n            stage.style.marginLeft = -RW / 2 + \"px\"; stage.style.marginTop = -RH / 2 + \"px\";\n            stage.style.transform = \"scale(\" + k + \")\";\n            var L = portrait\n              ? { cx: 360, cy: 600, bw: 600, bh: 420, heartY: 590, headY: 296, thanks: 900, sub: 984, cta: 1050 }\n              : { cx: 640, cy: 304, bw: 900, bh: 236, heartY: 286, headY: 120, thanks: 444, sub: 532, cta: 584 };\n\n            // Grid: near-square cells that fill the box, rows centered.\n            var count = names.length;\n            var cols = Math.max(1, Math.min(count, Math.round(Math.sqrt(count * L.bw / L.bh))));\n            var rows = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(count / cols));\n            var cellW = L.bw / cols, cellH = L.bh / rows;\n            var avSize = Math.min(84, Math.min(cellW, cellH) * 0.76);\n            var AV_START = 70, AV_DUR = 22, AV_WINDOW = 56;\n            var step = count > 1 ? Math.min(3, AV_WINDOW / (count - 1)) : 0;\n            var avs = names.map(function (nm, i) {\n              var r = Math.floor(i / cols), c = i % cols, rc = Math.min(cols, count - r * cols);\n              var x = L.cx - ((rc - 1) * cellW) / 2 + c * cellW, y = L.cy - ((rows - 1) * cellH) / 2 + r * cellH;\n              var d = el(\"div\", \"sg-av\", stage);\n              d.textContent = Array.from(nm)[0].toUpperCase();\n              var hue = (i * 47 + 20) % 360;\n              d.style.cssText += \"left:\" + x + \"px;top:\" + y + \"px;width:\" + avSize + \"px;height:\" + avSize + \"px;font-size:\" + avSize * 0.42 + \"px;background:hsl(\" + hue + \" 55% \" + (dark ? 42 : 58) + \"%)\";\n              return { d: d, x: x, y: y };\n            });\n\n            var HB = 168;\n            var heart = el(\"div\", \"sg-heart\", stage);\n            heart.style.cssText += \"left:\" + (L.cx - HB / 2) + \"px;top:\" + (L.heartY - HB / 2) + \"px;width:\" + HB + \"px;height:\" + HB + \"px\";\n            heart.innerHTML = '<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"' + HB + '\" height=\"' + HB + '\"><path id=\"sg-hp\" d=\"' + HEART + '\" pathLength=\"1\" fill=\"' + accent + '\" fill-opacity=\"0\" stroke=\"' + accent + '\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"1\" stroke-dashoffset=\"1\"/></svg>';\n            var hp = heart.querySelector(\"path\");\n\n            function words(parent, text, size, weight, color, spacing) {\n              var box = el(\"div\", \"sg-line\", parent);\n              box.style.width = RW + \"px\"; box.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; box.style.fontWeight = weight; box.style.color = color; box.style.letterSpacing = spacing;\n              return box;\n            }\n            var hBox = words(stage, \"\", 54, 600, T.fg, \"-0.05em\"); hBox.style.top = L.thanks + \"px\"; hBox.style.height = \"84px\"; hBox.style.lineHeight = \"84px\";\n            var hChars = Array.from(heading).map(function (ch) { var s = el(\"span\", \"sg-c\", hBox); s.textContent = ch; return s; });\n            var sBox = words(stage, \"\", 24, 500, T.muted, \"-0.03em\"); sBox.style.top = L.sub + \"px\"; sBox.style.height = \"36px\"; sBox.style.lineHeight = \"36px\";\n            var sWords = subline.split(\" \").filter(Boolean).map(function (w) { var s = el(\"span\", \"sg-w\", sBox); s.textContent = w; s.style.marginRight = \"0.25em\"; return s; });\n            var cta = el(\"div\", \"sg-cta\", stage); cta.style.top = L.cta + \"px\"; cta.style.width = RW + \"px\";\n            var pill = null, link = null;\n            if (ctaLabel) { pill = el(\"div\", \"sg-pill\", cta, '<svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"' + HEART + '\" fill=\"#fff\"/></svg>'); el(\"span\", \"\", pill).textContent = ctaLabel; }\n            if (linkText) { link = el(\"div\", \"sg-link\", cta); link.textContent = linkText; }\n\n            var DRAW_END = 40, PULSE_END = 62, DOCK_A = 52, DOCK_B = 84, THANK = 150, SUB = 166, CTA = 182;\n            var inOut = bez(0.42, 0, 0.58, 1);\n            function draw(fr) {\n              var f = fr; // frames already scaled by speed\n              hp.setAttribute(\"stroke-dashoffset\", 1 - interp(f, 0, DRAW_END, 0, 1, EASE_OUT));\n              hp.setAttribute(\"fill-opacity\", interp(f, DRAW_END - 8, PULSE_END, 0, 1));\n              var pulse = f < DRAW_END + 6 ? interp(f, DRAW_END - 2, DRAW_END + 6, 1, 0.9, inOut) : f < DRAW_END + 17 ? interp(f, DRAW_END + 6, DRAW_END + 17, 0.9, 1.06, inOut) : interp(f, DRAW_END + 17, PULSE_END, 1.06, 1, inOut);\n              var dock = interp(f, DOCK_A, DOCK_B, 0, 1, EASE_OUT);\n              heart.style.transform = \"translateY(\" + (L.headY - L.heartY) * dock + \"px) scale(\" + (1 - 0.62 * dock) * pulse + \")\";\n              avs.forEach(function (a, i) {\n                var p = interp(f, AV_START + i * step, AV_START + i * step + AV_DUR, 0, 1, EASE_OUT);\n                a.d.style.opacity = p;\n                a.d.style.transform = \"translate(-50%, calc(-50% + \" + (1 - p) * 14 + \"px))\";\n                a.d.style.filter = \"blur(\" + (1 - p) * 10 + \"px) grayscale(\" + (1 - p) + \")\";\n              });\n              hChars.forEach(function (s, i) {\n                var l = f - THANK - i;\n                var p = interp(l, 0, 27, 0, 1, EASE_OUT);\n                s.style.opacity = p;\n                s.style.transform = \"translateY(\" + interp(l, 0, 9, 16, 0, EASE_OUT) + \"px)\";\n                s.style.filter = \"blur(\" + interp(l, 0, 27, 12, 0, EASE_OUT) + \"px)\";\n              });\n              var total = 270, exitStart = Math.max(17 + sWords.length - 1, total - SUB - 14 - (sWords.length - 1));\n              sWords.forEach(function (s, i) {\n                var le = f - SUB - i, lx = f - SUB - exitStart - i;\n                var ep = interp(le, 0, 17, 0, 1, EASE_OUT), xp = interp(lx, 0, 14, 0, 1, EASE_IN);\n                s.style.opacity = ep * (1 - xp);\n                s.style.transform = \"translateY(\" + (interp(le, 0, 6, 10, 0, EASE_OUT) + interp(lx, 8, 14, 0, -14, EASE_IN)) + \"px)\";\n                s.style.filter = \"blur(\" + (interp(le, 0, 17, 6, 0, EASE_OUT) + interp(lx, 0, 14, 0, 8, EASE_IN)) + \"px)\";\n              });\n              if (pill) {\n                var cp = interp(f, CTA, CTA + 22, 0, 1, EASE_OUT);\n                pill.style.opacity = cp; pill.style.transform = \"translateY(\" + (1 - cp) * 12 + \"px)\"; pill.style.filter = \"blur(\" + (1 - cp) * 10 + \"px)\";\n              }\n              if (link) link.style.opacity = interp(f, CTA + 8, CTA + 30, 0, 1, EASE_OUT) * 0.9;\n            }\n\n            var seconds = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"9\");\n            var clock = { f: 0 };\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            tl.to(clock, { f: seconds * FPS * speed, duration: seconds, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.f); } }, 0);\n            draw(0);\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"supporter-grid\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
